ematica ","type":"text"},{"code":"FindHamiltonianPath","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Self-loops never help; one vertex is the trivial path. Pruning cuts only subtrees with no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"solution (an unvisited vertex unreachable, or left without a usable predecessor or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"successor), so it keeps the order. Without a start the search is run again from each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex in turn until one succeeds, so a graph with no Hamiltonian path costs n searches.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/hamiltonianpath()"},"doc://Tours/documentation/Tours/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/eulerianTrail(from:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"An Eulerian trail from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"start"},{"text":", or nil when none starts there (NetworkX","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"has_eulerian_path(G, source)"},{"text":"): ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"start"},{"text":" must be the vertex with out − in = 1, or, in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Eulerian graph, any vertex with an edge, or any vertex at all when there are no edges.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/euleriantrail(from:)","title":"eulerianTrail(from:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"eulerianTrail","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"from","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks5TrailV","text":"Trail","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"